OL,3,GNorth West
OL,4,
OL,5,CToday:FA murky start as any early mist
OL,6,Fand fog initially lifts to low cloud
OL,7,Fbefore breaking up through the
OL,8,Fmorning. Bright or sunny spells then
OL,9,Fbecome more prolonged during the day.
OL,10,FFeeling mild for the time of year.
OL,11,
OL,12,CTonight:FClear spells through the
OL,13,Fnight allowing temperatures to drop
OL,14,Faway quickly after dark. Mist or fog
OL,15,Fpatches likely forming in prone rural
OL,16,Fspots under light winds.
OL,17,
OL,18,CFriday:FFog or low cloud again slow to
OL,19,Fclear but once it does, another day of
OL,20,Fsunny spells and light winds follows.
OL,21,FFeeling pleasant in the sunshine.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
